  "recommended_local_dispatcher_policy": [
    "Bound message length, nesting, UTF8/string length and repeated count; do not silently truncate incompatible capability lists.",
    "Enforce destination service was advertised and successfully opened before setup; setup config index must identify supported advertised config; start must use accepted config; reject media outside active session.",
    "Encode proto2 required zero-valued status explicitly (ChannelOpenResponse OK: tag1=0); missing required is malformed rather than default success.",
    "Support protobuf unknown-field skipping and both packed/unpacked repeated scalar encodings; reject invalid wire type, overlong varint, length overflow/truncation.",
    "Do not confuse zero/default proto3 absence with required proto2 presence. Preserve uint64/int64 timestamps and signed session; int32 negative values use 10-byte sign-extended varint.",
    "Only commit state after complete successful decode. Reset AV session and outstanding credit on stop/shutdown; no inherited stale session or ACK against former stream.",
    "Place finite bounds on media queue. ACK one complete accepted media message only after receiver owns its bytes; avoid ACK when queue rejected/full. This queue admission policy is local design, not a verified phone contract.",
    "Serialize outbound TLS/framing callbacks; preserve channel plus encryption/type flags across fragments and validate minimum2-byte message ID before reading.",
    "Keep a narrow source-supported plaintext exception for ping/handshake/auth; do not accept arbitrary plaintext service or AV content after authentication.",
    "Treat unavailable host/video/audio backends as explicit open/setup FAIL, not successful native hardware capability."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Upstream sources are independently pinned; build compatibility and current Pixel interoperability are not proven.",
    "Source sender flag choices are observed static facts; strict receive enforcement/state policy are own recommendations.",
    "No real USB host, TLS phone handshake, Garmin display/DAC, H264 decoding speed, touchscreen or offline Maps projection test."
  ],
